<python>
cs_content_header = "Forces and Newton's Laws Practice Problems"
</python>

<style>
  body {
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    padding: 20px;
    background: #f9f9f9;
  }
  .card {
    background: white;
    border: 1px solid #ccc;
    padding: 16px;
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    border-radius: 10px;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.05);
  }
  .correct {
    color: green;
    font-weight: bold;
  }
  .incorrect {
    color: red;
    font-weight: bold;
  }
  input[type="text"] {
    width: 100%;
    padding: 8px;
    margin-top: 10px;
  }
  button {
    margin-top: 10px;
    padding: 8px 16px;
  }
</style>

<!-- Example -->
<div class="card">
  <h2>Example</h2>
  <p><strong>Example:</strong></p>
  <pre>
Newton's First Law states: An object will remain at rest or move with constant velocity unless acted upon by an external force.

Newton's Second Law is given by: 
F = ma
Where:
  F = Force (in Newtons)
  m = mass (in kilograms)
  a = acceleration (in m/s²)

Newton's Third Law states: For every action, there is an equal and opposite reaction.
</pre>
  <p>For example, if a 2 kg object accelerates at 3 m/s², the force acting on it is:<br>
  <code>F = 2 × 3 = 6 N</code></p>
</div>

<!-- Question 1 -->
<div class="card">
  <h2>Question 1</h2>
  <p><strong>Question:</strong> What is Newton's First Law also known as?</p>
  <input type="text" id="answer1" placeholder='Type your answer here'>
  <button onclick="checkAnswer('answer1', 'result1', 'law of inertia')">Submit</button>
  <div id="result1"></div>
</div>

<!-- Question 2 -->
<div class="card">
  <h2>Question 2</h2>
  <p><strong>Question:</strong> What is the force acting on a 4 kg object accelerating at 2 m/s²?</p>
  <input type="text" id="answer2" placeholder='Type your answer here'>
  <button onclick="checkAnswer('answer2', 'result2', '8')">Submit</button>
  <div id="result2"></div>
</div>

<!-- Question 3 -->
<div class="card">
  <h2>Question 3</h2>
  <p><strong>Question:</strong> What is the SI unit of force?</p>
  <input type="text" id="answer3" placeholder='Type your answer here'>
  <button onclick="checkAnswer('answer3', 'result3', 'newton')">Submit</button>
  <div id="result3"></div>
</div>

<!-- Question 4 -->
<div class="card">
  <h2>Question 4</h2>
  <p><strong>Question:</strong> State Newton's Third Law of Motion.</p>
  <input type="text" id="answer4" placeholder='Type your answer here'>
  <button onclick="checkAnswer('answer4', 'result4', 'for every action there is an equal and opposite reaction')">Submit</button>
  <div id="result4"></div>
</div>

<!-- Question 5 -->
<div class="card">
  <h2>Question 5</h2>
  <p><strong>Question:</strong> A force of 15 N acts on a 5 kg mass. What is the acceleration of the object?</p>
  <input type="text" id="answer5" placeholder='Type your answer here'>
  <button onclick="checkAnswer('answer5', 'result5', '3')">Submit</button>
  <div id="result5"></div>
</div>

<script>
  function checkAnswer(inputId, resultId, correctAnswer) {
    const userInput = document.getElementById(inputId).value.trim().toLowerCase();
    const resultDiv = document.getElementById(resultId);
    const expected = correctAnswer.toLowerCase();

    if (userInput === expected) {
      resultDiv.innerHTML = '<p class="correct">✅ Correct!</p>';
    } else {
      resultDiv.innerHTML = `<p class="incorrect">❌ Incorrect.</p><p>The correct answer is: <code>${correctAnswer}</code></p>`;
    }
  }
</script>
